\b 5.4 Recommendations for Future Work\b0\par
\par
1. Integrate monthly, district-level, or fishing-zone-level CMFRI landing data so that the model can learn finer spatiotemporal patterns.\par
2. Integrate Copernicus salinity, chlorophyll, currents, and mixed-layer-depth variables for stronger environmental representation.\par
3. Expand PFZ and field observation records containing species and observed fish lengths so that the juvenile model can train on more exact biological labels.\par
4. Enable native XGBoost by installing the required OpenMP runtime on macOS and benchmarking it against the Gradient Boosting fallback.\par
5. Introduce temporal forecasting, spatial interpolation, and uncertainty reporting for more realistic fisheries decision support.\par
6. Validate the system with real harbour or onboard observation campaigns to improve deployment readiness.\par
